WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.960
Want some tea?

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.110
We've got cake too, if you'd like.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.120
I think you'd like it, Hitomi.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.620
You worried about Takayama?

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.130
And the others, don't you mean?

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.320
I received a call earlier.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.420
Instructor Narita seemed
to be enjoying them.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.140
He doesn't change either, does he?

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.080
Do you think we've changed?

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:47.860
Well, you could do with learning to make your own tea, Hitomi.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.360
Takayama will be fine.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.650
He's the type that steps up when it matters.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:55.660
Oh?

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:59.160
I was never worried, though.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:02.870
Takayama!

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.110
You okay, Haruka?

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.940
Y-Yeah.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.820
Man, that was a surprise.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.280
I think a tree fell, blocking the line.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:07.950
You should have warned us!

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.460
The upgrades for the opening
of the Usui Abt railway

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.590
from Usui 3rd Bridge to Yokokawa are supposed to be nearly finished.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.930
It shouldn't be too dangerous.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.970
However, the slope's getting steeper.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.810
Not to mention we're not slowing down.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.700
Sakurai, Iwaizumi!

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.740
On it!

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.710
This ain't gonna work.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.250
The tunnel's too narrow.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.090
What now, Takayama?

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:01.920
The walls of the tunnel will keep us from tipping over. But once we're outside...

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.800
Deputy.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.930
We just need to get off the wall, right?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.680
Yeah.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.640
Roger that, Deputy!

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.060
Boo-yah!

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.830
Ow.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.790
Don't do crazy things on a running train!

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.750
But we made it through.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.170
Yeah, thanks.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.380
But don't do that again.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.630
Roger that, Deputy!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:45.130
Next is Tunnel 6, the longest on the old line.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.140
This is bad. We have to think of
a way to slow down.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:57.810
I know!

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.240
Iwaizumi, pedal with all your might.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.240
All right.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.660
Roger that!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.750
Wait, if he does that, we'll just speed up.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.170
I changed it over to power the cogs.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:27.430
Now the energy will just be used to spin the cogs underneath us, not the car's wheels.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.220
I get it. Abt traveling!

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.560
What's that?

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:38.850
Until 1963, the Shinetsu Main Line used rack rails, which are commonly seen in mountain railways.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.110
But this old line still uses it today.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.660
If we can get the cogs to
connect with that rail...

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.240
Right!

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:55.370
...we might just take
this curve without derailing!

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.040
There might be another impact, so grab on to something!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.720
Connect!

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.230
Don't give up.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.480
You're gonna be a train driver, right?

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:21.980
Takayama!

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.280
Try again.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.150
Pedal harder, Iwaizumi!

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:28.740
'Kay!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.160
Here we go.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.790
Connect!

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:54.970
It connected!

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:55.890
Yeah.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:01.480
But if we shoot through at
this speed, we're sure to go flying.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.980
As long as the Abt system
is connected, we should be fine.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.380
Turn!

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:40.520
Yes!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.270
The plan was a success!

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.280
You can stop pedaling now.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:49.780
Cool.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.330
You okay, Iwaizumi?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.580
I think I hurt it kicking the wall.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.000
All right. Just take it easy for now.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.210
Thanks.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.220
This is the Usui 3rd Bridge.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.680
Feels like we're running through the sky.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.060
We're really high up.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.860
Tunnel 5 is coming up.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:52.510
There's bound to be a lot of strain on the Abt system from doing this.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.880
Will it last till Yokokawa?

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.270
Takayama.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.660
T-Takayama!

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:23.910
Sakurai!

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.800
Be careful, Sakurai.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.010
Sorry.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.150
This is the last tunnel.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.010
We're through all the tunnels.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:17.840
Yes!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.180
The Abt system broke.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:29.440
Good thing it didn't break
a few seconds earlier.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:49.290
We'll be merging with the
new line's outbound line soon.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:04.010
Just the S-curve before Yokokawa. Easy peasy.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.770
Where do you get off being so confident?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.520
I almost died because of your driving.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:13.520
Sorry. But it all worked out, right?

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.570
Are we really gonna be okay?

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.150
We just lost a piece of the train.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.450
We'll be fine.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:26.790
The Abt system may be broken,
but the slope over here is pretty gentle.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.580
The Unit D dynamic braking
should see us though.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.300
It couldn't handle the extra strain.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.090
Wh-What now?

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.840
We'll just have to rely on this.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:49.680
Huh?

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.890
That's weird.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:52.310
What's wrong?

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.560
I don't know.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:57.320
I haven't been using the brake much, so it shouldn't be broken.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.230
But it's not working as well as before.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:05.450
Maybe we're experiencing a brake fade.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.500
Then what do we do?

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:14.720
Not using it for a while should
allow it to cool down and recover.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.810
We're definitely gonna need
the brake to stop at the station.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.470
I want to save it till then.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.180
Hey.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.100
How many more curves are there?

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.480
Two. One should be coming up soon.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:39.230
Iwaizumi, drive for me.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:41.110
No can do, man.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.070
You only have to operate the car once.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:47.070
Pull on the brake as hard as you can
when we get to the station.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.780
Sounds possible!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:50.240
Sakurai.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.830
We'll take these curves by shifting the car's center of gravity.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:56.460
I'll replace Iwaizumi. Help me out.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.210
You sure you can do this, Takayama?

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.170
It's pretty scary stuff.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:08.100
I don't want to, but it's our only option.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:09.890
Right.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:12.520
Two curves left!

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.030
Takayama, get moving.

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.490
R-Right.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.880
If you don't focus, you'll get flung right off.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:47.510
You know how people handle roller coasters?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.970
They scream their hearts out!

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:02.150
I'll be a train driver, just you see!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.920
Not a bad effort, considering.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.340
Not bad, huh?

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:24.420
Next up is the last curve,
but it's a doozy.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:24.840
Got it.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:31.260
We're on the longest straight track
between Yokokawa and Karuizawa.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.350
The Maruyama Straight, huh?

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:39.020
The slope's gentle, but it's still there, so we'll be speeding up.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.310
We're almost at the last curve.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.360
Sakurai, let's go!

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.860
Roger that, Deputy.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.580
It's really pulling away from us!

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.880
Damn it.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:07.840
It's not working!

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.760
K-Koumi?

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.890
I can park my butt on the side too!

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.180
Hup.

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.930
Count me in, too!

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.110
Let's go!

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:27.990
Turn!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.370
We did it!

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.410
That's Yokokawa Station!

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.670
The signal's not red.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.460
Yellow means caution.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.340
That's the signal that
it's okay to enter the station.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.380
Oh, Iwaizumi!

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.340
The brake!

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:51.550
Got it!

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:03.690
Stop!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.690
S-Sorry.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.190
You pulled too hard!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:11.700
I got this!

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:14.240
Our last hope!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.330
Hup!

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.620
Taste the Iwaizumi Brake!

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.170
You're kidding.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:29.170
That's amazing, Iwaizumi!

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:40.430
Hey! Hit the brakes!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.570
You've gotta jump. Go, Haruka!

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:49.690
Okay!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.360
Takayama, help her.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:53.860
Got it.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.700
Let's go, Koumi.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:00.790
Yeah!

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.500
And jump!

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.360
Is the container okay?

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:32.780
It's fine.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:34.610
Thank goodness.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:42.490
Ms. Oito of the Japanese Organs
Transit System entrusted us with this.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.250
Thank you very much.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:46.500
It's yours now.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.500
We need to get moving.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.380
I'm sorry, Takayama.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:59.470
This is all because of my selfishness.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:04.890
See, I lost someone important to me
long ago because of something like this.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.640
So I couldn't just stand idly by.

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:07.890
That's why?

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.610
Well, don't worry. I'm sure we made it.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:12.900
Hey.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:15.360
How long you lovebirds
gonna hold each other?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:19.700
Takayama, you don't deserve half the fortune that comes your way.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.280
Why?

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.540
That's mission complete, right?

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:32.290
What?

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.340
We're all pretty beat up, huh?

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.050
Sorry. I'm not really fit to lead us.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:43.640
That's about all you can expect from a Deputy like me.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:49.020
Not to mention when I joined JNR, I wanted to be a train driver, not part of the PSF.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:53.820
But now I <i>am</i> part of the PSF.

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.490
That's the truth.

00:18:57.650 --> 00:19:01.820
So would you please stick with me in K4?

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.290
Of course, Deputy.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:10.750
Roger that!

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:14.090
Awaiting orders, Deputy!

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.420
Fine, dummy.

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:22.590
Thank you.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.930
Training complete. Training complete.

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:32.900
Hakusan Express safely ran from Karuizawa to Yokokawa.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.980
No large impacts.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:37.190
No damage to the coupling.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.700
All of a sudden you guys are competent.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.870
That was some real teamwork.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:49.450
Something good happen during your break?

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.080
N-No, nothing really.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:56.550
Well, whether you guys make up by duking it out or smooching it out,

00:19:56.550 --> 00:20:00.300
as long as your results are good
I don't give a damn.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.130
W-We didn'tвЂ”

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.050
Takayama.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:03.720
Yes, sir!

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.680
I'm giving you a barely
passing grade this time,

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.600
but you've got a lot to learn before you're a real driver.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:11.310
Yes, sir!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.770
So come back sometime.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.900
I'll put you through the wringer.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:18.480
Thank you, sir!

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.110
Dismissed!

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.700
Thank you very much!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:27.240
I need food <i>now</i> ! I didn't eat nearly enough!

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:32.120
Eyes front. We have to hurry or we'll be late to Noa's concert.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:34.330
And she'll get mad at me.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:38.040
Sasshou, it's amazing how you can make friends with literally anyone.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.920
It's not like that.

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:42.470
Besides, Noa's a rival.

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.430
Rival in what?

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:45.840
That's a secret!

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:47.600
What's up?

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:49.810
Nothing.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:54.600
Oh yeah, I heard JNR was going to
reimburse you guys for the clothes.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.320
You want that dress?

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.480
N-Nah.

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:03.320
I think I'll go with something
easier to move in.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.570
Why?

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:08.700
"Why"? Because frills aren't for me.

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:11.950
Really? I think you look pretty good in them.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:12.830
Huh?

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.250
J-Just a little!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.840
B-But you <i>were</i> cute.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.510
What're you saying, dummy?

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:26.220
But if you say so, maybe I'll
look for another one.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:28.850
Aoi!

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:30.760
Over here!

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.810
Look at these! They're so cute!

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.100
Coming!

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:43.240
Takayama, I'm joining the Public Security Force.

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:46.990
And I'm joining the Driver Division.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:53.540
Guess I'll have to protect whatever sorry train you end up driving.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:59.500
We'll both have to pass this OJT and get hired by JNR first, though.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.290
I'll be fine.

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:05.170
You might be screwed with those driving skills, though.

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:06.300
What're you talking about?

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:08.800
Do you know how many acts of God I had to deal with?

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:09.930
I wasn't even tryingвЂ”

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:43.690
The Hokutosei, Japan's first luxury express sleeper train,

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:46.860
is made up of a dining car, lounge cars, and private sleeping quarters.

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:50.860
The special express sleeper train runs the
whole length between Ueno and Sapporo

00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:53.990
for an amazing travel distance
of 1215 kilometers!

00:23:53.990 --> 00:23:54.820
Oh, sorry.

00:23:55.160 --> 00:23:57.700
You were gonna explain that, right, Naoto?

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:01.160
Huh? What's the matter? You're all stiff.

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:03.000
I'll just finish on my own, then.

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:07.340
Rail Wars, Episode Ten: Will You Keep It a Secret?

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:09.460
That's a promise, Naoto!
